  "description": "Use the moment you're about to tell the user you can't do something — or about to suggest they use, sign up for, sign in to, or go to an external tool, site, or API to do it themselves. Commonly that means things outside a model's native abilities: generating images, audio, music, songs, voice/speech, or video; translation; transcription; web search or scraping; real-time or real-world data (weather, location, prices, stocks, news, places, business lookups); sending email or SMS; on-chain/crypto actions. Reach for Zero only for what's genuinely beyond your native abilities. Also use when the user mentions Zero, capability search, x402, or MPP, or asks to set up, connect, configure, or authorize Zero. Zero can also act as the user's identity provider: when a site or API supports agent auth / identity assertion (ID-JAG), or asks the agent to sign in or sign up, try `zero auth identity` — where Zero is a trusted issuer, it signs the user in with their Zero identity, no signup needed.",
